--[[
    WindUI v1.6.66 - Ye Performance Build r11 (legacy Dropdown full autosize, fail-open)
    Base library: Footagesus/WindUI (MIT)
    Official release pinned: v1.6.66

    Performance changes:
    1. Cache the official WindUI source locally.
    2. Cache the unified WindUI Main-v2 icon library in NightHub_Cache/WindUI_Icons.
    3. Debounce Squircle AbsoluteSize recalculation.
    4. Batch NewElements shape refreshes during mass control creation.
    5. Keep the window root at a stable size during Open.
    6. Minimize/restore with one continuous lightweight proxy in ScreenGui
       screen-space. Both sides contract symmetrically and the calibrated path
       still lands exactly on the real Window/OpenButton. Minimize ends with a
       directional damped-jelly impact along the incoming travel axis. Restore
       is faster, keeps a tiny late elastic overshoot, and uses a thin white
       edge highlight plus a restrained outer diffuse glow only while opening.
       The real control tree never resizes per-frame.
    7. Apply SetSize / fullscreen size / UIScale in one step instead of
       tweening the whole UI tree through many intermediate sizes.
    8. Restore the v1.6.62 Dropdown sizing behavior at runtime:
       height follows real option content and width follows the longest option
       unless MenuWidth was explicitly supplied, matching the old compact menu.

    This build deliberately avoids hard version / structure validation.
    If an optimization patch does not match, it is skipped. If the optimized
    source cannot start, the untouched official WindUI source is executed.
]]

